\ crypto/sha512_test.fam — the SHA-512 module (crypto/sha512.fam) against
\ Python's hashlib (the values written by this file's generator, in the
\ commit that added it): digests of 0, 3, 111, 112 and 300 bytes (one
\ block, the padding's edge, several); HMAC-SHA512 with a short key and
\ one over a block (hashed first); PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512 at 1 and 2
\ iterations, and BIP39's own (2,048, salt "mnemonicTREZOR").  Prints
\ "sha512: N as expected, M not".

: tpas variable ;  : tfai variable ;  : tbuf variable ;  : tbn variable ;  : tex variable ;  : tout variable ;
: tchk  swap if drop tpas @ 1 lit + tpas ! else "sha512: " puts puts 0A lit putc tfai @ 1 lit + tfai ! then ;   \ ( flag str -- )
\ tb ( c -- )  a byte to the input; tx ( c -- )  a byte to the expected.
: tb  tbuf @ tbn @ + c!  tbn @ 1 lit + tbn ! ;
: txp variable ;
: tx  tex @ txp @ + c!  txp @ 1 lit + txp ! ;
: tsame  ( a b n -- flag )  -1 lit swap 0 lit do 2 lit pick i + c@ 2 lit pick i + c@ = and loop nip nip ;
800 lit alloc tbuf !  80 lit alloc tex !  80 lit alloc tout !
: tnew  0 lit tbn !  0 lit txp ! ;

